      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $B=\\{1,2,2,3,4,5,5\\}$, then $|B|=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $B$ is the number of elements in $B.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $B:$\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,5\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $B$ has $5$ elements, its cardinality is $|B|=\\text{5}.$",
